  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Calculate $\\int 4{cot}^{2}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x.$",
  "worked_solution": "In this case, we have to use the identity  $1+{cot}^{2}\u2061x={csc}^{2}\u2061x.$ Rearranging this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cot}^{2}\u2061x & ={csc}^{2}\u2061x-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4{cot}^{2}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 4({csc}^{2}\u2061x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (4{csc}^{2}\u2061x-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x-4x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
